<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermann Billung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 973</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermann Billung was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> noble whom Otto I entrusted around 936 with command against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, the frontier later called the Billung March. He governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> for Otto during the king's absences and is counted as the first Billung duke of Saxony. His family held the ducal title until 1106.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermann-billung.jpg" alt="Hermann Billung" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermann_Billung.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
